//? Title: GhostNet: Intrinsic Maps and Cheap Feature Generation
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Ghost modules derive additional maps from a smaller intrinsic representation. We inspect
ceiling/trimming and exact derivatives, verify released model budgets and complete gradients,
then explicitly fit all sixteen CIFAR bottlenecks through tensor Adam.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.4_efficient_and_mobile_architectures/ghostnet.cpp`.

> The method

A ratio-s ghost module produces ceil(Cout/s) intrinsic maps with a primary 1×1/BN, then
uses a depthwise 3×3 multiplier s-1 to generate more maps. Concatenation puts intrinsic
maps first and trims the tail to Cout; odd requested widths therefore compute some unused
maps. Optional ReLU follows both BN stages. The controlled fixture disables it so a primary
identity and cheap gain two yield [x0,x1,x2,2x0,2x1] for five outputs, with exact input
sum derivatives [3,3,1] and zero data gradient for the discarded generated x2 filter.

For Cout divisible by s, primary kernel k, cheap kernel d and Cin=c, the dense/ghost
kernel-product ratio is

$$R=\frac{s c k^2}{c k^2+(s-1)d^2}.$$
\alttext(Cheap generation replaces many dense spatial products, with a remaining depthwise overhead.)

At 160→960, s=2,k=1,d=3 this is 1.893491, checked from actual kernel sizes and output
shape MACs. It is an arithmetic/kernel-storage ratio, not measured runtime or a compressed
model-file ratio. BN, activations, memory traffic, ceiling overhead and device kernels can
change practical costs. Complete learned totals below include BN and biases separately.

Each bottleneck uses activated Ghost1, a strided depthwise/BN when needed, optional pooled
SE with ReLU/hard sigmoid, linear Ghost2 and shortcut addition without post-ReLU. Dimension
changes use a depthwise/BN plus pointwise/BN shortcut. SE reduction aligns mid*.25 to four.
The full network has sixteen released bottlenecks, a 3×3/2 stem, final 1×1/BN/ReLU to
scaled 960, global pooling, biased 1×1/ReLU to fixed 1280, dropout .2 and a classifier.
Widths align to four. Full widths .5/1/1.3 have 2587292/5182508/7358820 learned scalars
and 10984/21968/28536 moving scalars, with 42.33/141.15/227.00 million counted MACs at 224.
He-uniform fan-in is an initialization adaptation; BN learns gamma/beta with epsilon 1e-5.

The complete full-width backward probe uses 64-pixel synthetic inputs without dropout. It
shifts BN betas/SE biases, retaining every bottleneck. A BN shift is redundant only when its
consumers linearly pass channel constants into later training BN. Projection-depthwise shifts,
strided no-SE depthwise shifts and eligible residual-stream shifts are identified from the actual
unit topology, separately from nonredundant gradients. Zero gradients there are not disconnected
filters. Moving updates are disabled for this diagnostic, not for the dataset fit.

The visible fit retains full width/all sixteen bottlenecks on original 32×32 CIFAR images,
changing only the stem stride and class count. It has 3914318 learned and 21968 moving scalars.
Ten batch-eight epochs use 64 fit/32 validation/32 official-test rows, Adam(.001), explicit
kernel L2=.0001/2 and independent padded crops/flips. Validation selects paired learned/moving
state checkpoints before testing. The tensor library performs preprocessing, forward, loss and
optimization. This tiny single-seed experiment differs from the larger source fit and published
ImageNet training; it cannot reproduce benchmark accuracy or establish architecture superiority.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/ghostnet_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/ghostnet_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/ghostnet_concept.tikz > build/ghostnet_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/ghostnet_concept.svg build/ghostnet_concept.dvi > build/ghostnet_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
